<!--
  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
  DEV ONLY, this machine. The simulated PSTN trunk, as a plain <extension>
  inside the aicc context's include point — not a second <context> block,
  which FreeSWITCH would ignore.

  The caller id the far end sees comes from the platform: click-to-dial sets
  effective_caller_id_number on the agent's leg from the number marked as the
  deployment's default outbound one, and this passes it onward to the trunk
  leg. It used to be pinned to $${pstn_gateway_caller_id}, which quietly beat
  whatever the platform had chosen — the Numbers page said 95555 was what the
  callee would see, and every call went out as 95001.

  The pattern is any 7-to-16-digit number, optionally + prefixed. It matched
  only the ten test terminals behind the simulator until 2026-09-09, when it
  was widened to the general form and verified on a live call to a US number.
  The narrow pattern was there to keep a mistyped number a dialplan miss
  rather than a call into a trunk that cannot complete it; the trunk now
  reaches the real PSTN, so the numbers it can complete are no longer a list
  this file could hold.

  The codec pin rides the trunk leg itself, as it does on the bot leg. A PSTN
  speaks G.711 and nothing else, while $${global_codec_prefs} opens with OPUS,
  so an unpinned offer is answered with 488 and the call never rings. Pinning
  only the b-leg leaves the caller free to speak whatever it likes; the switch
  transcodes between the two.

  Two gates come first, and they exist so a call never goes round the loop. A
  call that arrived from the carrier through FreeSBC carries
  X-FreeSBC-Carrier (inbound calls were captured arriving with
  X-FreeSBC-Carrier: pstn), and a call this switch already sent out carries
  X-FSBC-Out, which the bridge below stamps on the outbound INVITE so the SBC,
  and this dialplan if the call comes back, can recognise the switch's own leg.
  Either header means the call must not be placed into the gateway again. Each
  gate is a condition on the header being empty (^$, which an absent header
  expands to) with no action and the default break of on-false: a header that
  is present fails the gate, which ends this extension before any of the
  break="never" conditions below can set anything or place a call.

  Only calls this dialplan places carry X-FSBC-Out. An AI outbound call does
  not come through here: the application originates it straight to
  AICC_OUTBOUND_ENDPOINT (sofia/gateway/<gw>/%s), and the application names no
  SBC vendor's header, so its INVITE carries no marker. That is by design. If
  the carrier reflects such a call back, it arrives with X-FreeSBC-Carrier and
  lands in the public context, so the first gate is the one that holds on that
  path. Revisit this before outbound campaigns make that path the main one.

  Then three conditions rather than one, because a fallback needs somewhere to be
  written before it can be overwritten: the first sets it, the second replaces
  it when the leg carries a number of its own (break="never" so a leg that
  carries none simply falls through), the third places the call.
-->
<include>
  <extension name="pstn_gateway_outbound">
      <condition field="${sip_h_X-FreeSBC-Carrier}" expression="^$"/>
      <condition field="${sip_h_X-FSBC-Out}" expression="^$"/>
      <condition field="destination_number" expression="^\+?[0-9]{7,16}$" break="never">
        <action application="set" data="trunk_clid=$${pstn_gateway_caller_id}"/>
      </condition>
      <condition field="${effective_caller_id_number}" expression="^([0-9]+)$" break="never">
        <action application="set" data="trunk_clid=$1"/>
      </condition>
      <condition field="destination_number" expression="^(\+?[0-9]{7,16})$">
        <action application="set" data="hangup_after_bridge=true"/>
        <action application="set" data="continue_on_fail=false"/>
        <!-- Records the placement under the same UTC-dated key the application
             looks the object up by, if the DID the far end will see has
             recording enabled. Runs after trunk_clid is decided and before the
             trunk leg exists, and never fails the call. -->
        <action application="lua" data="aicc_outbound.lua"/>
        <action application="set" data="sip_h_X-FSBC-Out=1"/>
        <action application="bridge" data="{absolute_codec_string=PCMU,PCMA,origination_caller_id_number=${trunk_clid},origination_caller_id_name=${trunk_clid}}sofia/gateway/pstn_gateway/$1"/>
      </condition>
    </extension>
</include>
